  "description": "{% if claude %}/builtin-gh:merge-pr{% else %}$builtin-gh:merge-pr{% endif %} only. Merge a pull request the way its base branch requires. Without a merge queue it merges directly, or arms auto-merge while checks run. With a merge queue it enqueues the PR and watches it until it lands. When a merge-group check fails, it dequeues early once eviction is certain. On an eviction it diagnoses the failure, fixes and pushes, then re-arms auto-merge so GitHub requeues the PR. A PR queued behind one it conflicts with waits for that PR: resolve and requeue if it merged, requeue unchanged if it failed. Use when the user explicitly asks to merge, land, ship, or queue a PR, or to watch a queued PR through to merge. Never use the merge as a step of another workflow unless the user asked for it, and never bypass the queue with admin privileges.",
